# NE555 astable multivibrator blinking an LED — the classic first IC
# circuit. Exercises the generic `ic` body with named pins on both sides,
# wire crossings (no dot = no connection) and a three-branch ground rail.
circuit 555 astable blinker

ic 14 8 h U1 NE555 l:GND,TRIG,OUT,RESET r:VCC,DIS,THR,CV

# supply rails
wire 8 2  25 2
vcc 13 2
dot 13 2
wire 4 21  25 21
gnd 14 21
dot 14 21

# supply pins: VCC and RESET up to the rail, GND down
wire 17.8 5.6  22 5.6  22 2
dot 22 2
wire 10.2 10.4  8 10.4  8 2
wire 10.2 5.6  6 5.6  6 21
dot 6 21

# timing network: VCC -> R1 -> DIS -> R2 -> THR/TRIG -> C1 -> GND
resistor 25 5 v R1 10k
wire 17.8 7.2  21 7.2  21 8  25 8
dot 25 8
resistor 25 11 v R2 47k
wire 17.8 8.8  23 8.8  23 14
wire 10.2 7.2  9 7.2  9 12.5  23 12.5  23 14
dot 23 14
wire 23 14  25 14
dot 25 14
wire 25 14  25 15
capacitor 25 18 v C1 10u

# output stage: OUT -> series resistor -> LED -> ground rail
wire 10.2 8.8  4 8.8  4 9
resistor 4 12 v R3 330
led 4 18 r90 D1 red
